Rem Capability: buzzer
Rem ==================================================================
Rem seedbuzzer.shoddy — reckoner seed: buzzer.shoddy, a tune from the
Rem entry line
Rem
Rem 1 "T140 O5 CDEC CDEC EFG EFG" BUZZPLAY, and the mill plays it.
Rem
Rem NOT A RESOURCE, WHICH MAKES THIS THE ODD ONE OUT of the seeds that
Rem reach a device. A window and a file are opened, held and shut; a
Rem sound is FIRED. SOUNDQUEUE takes a channel NUMBER — one of eight
Rem that always exist — and returns as soon as the notes are queued, so
Rem there is nothing to bind, nothing to name and nothing to CLOSE. The
Rem resource table does not come into it.
Rem
Rem ---- WHAT DID HAVE TO CHANGE, AND WHERE ---------------------------
Rem
Rem buzzer's MML parser aborted five ways and its note-name reader two
Rem more, and R3.5(a) does not allow a bridged word that can end the
Rem session. There was no guarded builtin to build on, because the
Rem parse is not in the runtime — it is in the MACHINE.
Rem
Rem So buzzer.shoddy grew the tree's first machine-level guarded twins:
Rem TryMmlNotes and TryNoteMidi answer a Result, and MmlNotes and
Rem NoteMidi are those answers with the Err turned back into the abort
Rem they always were. One set of rules, not a parser and a validator
Rem that drift apart — which is the whole reason it was worth rewriting
Rem a working parser rather than checking the string twice.
Rem
Rem AND ONE RUNTIME ADDITION, for the one sound fault nothing could
Rem pre-flight. SOUNDQUEUE refuses more than five minutes queued ahead
Rem on a channel, and until SOUNDQUEUED there was no way to ask how much
Rem was already in front of you. A word that measured its own score and
Rem still could not see the queue would be guessing.
Rem
Rem ---- THE SILENCE IS NOT AN ERROR ----------------------------------
Rem
Rem With no audio device every sound word is a no-op rather than a
Rem failure, so BUZZPLAY answers the same at a prompt with speakers and
Rem one without. That is buzzer's own contract and this seed keeps it:
Rem a session is told when its MUSIC is wrong and never when the machine
Rem it is running on has no sound.
Rem ==================================================================

Include "buzzer.shoddy"
Include "cuttle.shoddy"
Include "reckoner.shoddy"
Include "seq.shoddy"

Rem ---- the shared guards -------------------------------------------------

Rem Eight channels, and they are the runtime's own count rather than a
Rem number chosen here.
Def BzChannels() As Number
    8

Def BzWhyChannel(word As String, ch As Number) As String
    If ch < 1 Or ch > BzChannels() Or ch <> Floor(ch) Then
        word & ": THE CHANNEL MUST BE A WHOLE NUMBER FROM 1 TO " & Str(BzChannels())
    Else
        ""

Rem SOUNDQUEUE refuses more than five minutes queued ahead, and that is
Rem the one sound fault a caller cannot see coming without asking. The
Rem score's own length is measured, added to what is already playing,
Rem and the whole thing refused before a single note is queued — because
Rem a tune half queued is a tune that has already started.
Def BzCapMs() As Number
    5 * 60000

Def BzWhyRoom(word As String, ch As Number, ms As Number) As String
    If SoundQueued(ch) + ms > BzCapMs() Then
        word & ": THAT WOULD PUT MORE THAN " & Str(BzCapMs() / 60000) & " MINUTES AHEAD ON CHANNEL " & Str(ch) & " — LET SOME PLAY, OR " & Str(ch) & " BUZZSTOP"
    Else
        ""

Def BzTotalMs(ns As List Of BuzzerNote) As Number
    Fold(Map(ns, MsOfNote), 0, +)

Def MsOfNote(n As BuzzerNote) As Number
    Ms(n)

Rem ---- BUZZPLAY ----------------------------------------------------------

Def BzSeedPlay(st As RckState) As RckState
    Let s1 = RckReg(st, "BUZZPLAY", 2, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => BzPlay(vs)), "( ch mml -- )", "Play an MML tune on channel 1 to 8. A-G are notes, # and - sharpen and flatten, a digit is a length, O sets the octave, T the tempo, L the default length, P or R a rest. Returns as soon as the tune is queued.")
    Let s2 = RckReg(s1, "BUZZTONE", 3, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => BzTone(vs)), "( ch hz ms -- )", "Queue one tone of hz hertz for ms milliseconds. A frequency of 0 is a rest.")
    Let s3 = RckReg(s2, "BUZZNOTE", 3, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => BzNote(vs)), "( ch name ms -- )", "Queue one named note — \"C4\", \"F#3\", \"Bb5\" — for ms milliseconds. C4 is middle C.")
    Let s4 = RckReg(s3, "BUZZFREQ", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => BzFreq(vs)), "( name -- hz )", "The frequency of a named note in hertz, and nothing is played. \"A4\" is 440.")
    Let s5 = RckReg(s4, "BUZZLENGTH", 1, RckPure(Fn(vs) => BzLength(vs)), "( mml -- ms )", "How long that tune would take, in milliseconds, without playing a note of it. The way to check a score before committing it to a channel.")
    Let s5a = RckReg(s5, "BUZZQUEUED", 1, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => BzQueued(vs)), "( ch -- ms )", "How far ahead that channel is already queued, in milliseconds, and 0 once it has drained. BUZZLENGTH measures a tune; this measures what is in front of it.")
    Let s6 = RckReg(s5a, "BUZZSTOP", 1, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => BzStop(vs)), "( ch -- )", "Stop channel 1 to 8 at once and throw away whatever it had queued.")
    Let s7 = RckReg(s6, "BUZZGAIN", 2, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => BzGain(vs)), "( ch v -- )", "How loud that channel is, from 0 to 1. Sticky until set again.")
    RckReg(s7, "BUZZWAVE", 2, RckTouch(Fn(vs) => BzWave(vs)), "( ch name -- )", "The channel's waveform: \"square\", \"triangle\" or \"sine\". Sticky until set again.")

Def BzPlay(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(RckWholeArg("BUZZPLAY", Nth(vs, 1)), RckTextArg("BUZZPLAY", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(ch), Ok(mml))
            BzPlayChannel(ch, mml)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZPLAY needs a channel and an MML STRING")

Def BzPlayChannel(ch As Number, mml As String) As RckWork
    If BzWhyChannel("BUZZPLAY", ch) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(BzWhyChannel("BUZZPLAY", ch))
    Else
        BzPlayParsed(ch, TryMmlNotes(mml))

Def BzPlayParsed(ch As Number, r As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(ns)
            BzPlayRoom(ch, ns)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad("BUZZPLAY: " & w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZPLAY did not answer")

Def BzPlayRoom(ch As Number, ns As List Of BuzzerNote) As RckWork
    If BzWhyRoom("BUZZPLAY", ch, BzTotalMs(ns)) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(BzWhyRoom("BUZZPLAY", ch, BzTotalMs(ns)))
    Else
        BzPlayed(ch, ns)

Def BzPlayed(ch As Number, ns As List Of BuzzerNote) As RckWork
    PlayNotes(ch, ns)
    RckVals({ })

Rem ---- BUZZTONE and BUZZNOTE ---------------------------------------------

Def BzTone(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case BzThree("BUZZTONE", vs)
        Case Ok(ns)
            BzToneAt("BUZZTONE", Nth(ns, 1), Nth(ns, 2), Nth(ns, 3))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZTONE did not answer")

Def BzThree(word As String, vs As List Of Cell) As Result
    Select Case Pair(RckNumArg(word, Nth(vs, 1)), RckNumArg(word, Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(a), Ok(b))
            BzThird(word, a, b, RckNumArg(word, Nth(vs, 3)))
        Case Else
            Err(word & " needs three NUMBERs", 0)

Def BzThird(word As String, a As Number, b As Number, r As Result) As Result
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(c)
            Ok({ a, b, c })
        Case Err(w, at)
            Err(w, at)
        Case Else
            Err(word & " did not answer", 0)

Rem SoundQueue refuses a negative frequency and a negative duration, so
Rem both are asked here — and the whole thing is checked before the one
Rem note is queued, for the same reason a tune is.
Def BzToneAt(word As String, ch As Number, hz As Number, ms As Number) As RckWork
    If BzWhyChannel(word, ch) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(BzWhyChannel(word, ch))
    Else
        BzToneSound(word, ch, hz, ms)

Def BzToneSound(word As String, ch As Number, hz As Number, ms As Number) As RckWork
    If hz < 0 Then
        RckWorkBad(word & ": A FREQUENCY CANNOT BE NEGATIVE — 0 IS A REST")
    Else
        BzToneTimed(word, ch, hz, ms)

Def BzToneTimed(word As String, ch As Number, hz As Number, ms As Number) As RckWork
    If ms < 0 Then
        RckWorkBad(word & ": A NOTE CANNOT LAST LESS THAN NO TIME")
    Else
        BzToneRoom(word, ch, hz, ms)

Def BzToneRoom(word As String, ch As Number, hz As Number, ms As Number) As RckWork
    If BzWhyRoom(word, ch, ms) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(BzWhyRoom(word, ch, ms))
    Else
        BzToneQueued(ch, hz, ms)

Def BzToneQueued(ch As Number, hz As Number, ms As Number) As RckWork
    SoundQueue(ch, hz, ms)
    RckVals({ })

Def BzNote(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(RckWholeArg("BUZZNOTE", Nth(vs, 1)), RckTextArg("BUZZNOTE", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(ch), Ok(name))
            BzNoteMs(ch, name, Nth(vs, 3))
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZNOTE needs a channel, a note name and a length in ms")

Def BzNoteMs(ch As Number, name As String, mc As Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckNumArg("BUZZNOTE", mc)
        Case Ok(ms)
            BzNoteNamed(ch, name, ms, TryNoteMidi(name))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZNOTE did not answer")

Def BzNoteNamed(ch As Number, name As String, ms As Number, r As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(midi)
            BzToneAt("BUZZNOTE", ch, MidiFreq(midi), ms)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad("BUZZNOTE: " & w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZNOTE did not answer")

Rem ---- the two that play nothing -----------------------------------------

Def BzFreq(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("BUZZFREQ", First(vs))
        Case Ok(name)
            BzFreqOf(name, TryNoteMidi(name))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZFREQ did not answer")

Def BzFreqOf(name As String, r As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(midi)
            RckVals({ CutNum(MidiFreq(midi)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad("BUZZFREQ: " & w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZFREQ did not answer")

Rem The score measured without being played, which is what makes the
Rem queue cap something a session can work with rather than run into.
Def BzLength(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckTextArg("BUZZLENGTH", First(vs))
        Case Ok(mml)
            BzLengthOf(TryMmlNotes(mml))
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZLENGTH did not answer")

Def BzLengthOf(r As Result) As RckWork
    Select Case r
        Case Ok(ns)
            RckVals({ CutNum(BzTotalMs(ns)) })
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad("BUZZLENGTH: " & w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZLENGTH did not answer")

Rem ---- the channel settings ----------------------------------------------

Def BzQueued(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckWholeArg("BUZZQUEUED", First(vs))
        Case Ok(ch)
            BzQueuedAt(ch)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZQUEUED did not answer")

Def BzQueuedAt(ch As Number) As RckWork
    If BzWhyChannel("BUZZQUEUED", ch) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(BzWhyChannel("BUZZQUEUED", ch))
    Else
        RckVals({ CutNum(SoundQueued(ch)) })

Def BzStop(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case RckWholeArg("BUZZSTOP", First(vs))
        Case Ok(ch)
            BzStopAt(ch)
        Case Err(w, at)
            RckWorkBad(w)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZSTOP did not answer")

Def BzStopAt(ch As Number) As RckWork
    If BzWhyChannel("BUZZSTOP", ch) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(BzWhyChannel("BUZZSTOP", ch))
    Else
        BzStopped(ch)

Def BzStopped(ch As Number) As RckWork
    SoundStop(ch)
    RckVals({ })

Def BzGain(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(RckWholeArg("BUZZGAIN", Nth(vs, 1)), RckNumArg("BUZZGAIN", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(ch), Ok(v))
            BzGainAt(ch, v)
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZGAIN needs a channel and a loudness from 0 to 1")

Def BzGainAt(ch As Number, v As Number) As RckWork
    If BzWhyChannel("BUZZGAIN", ch) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(BzWhyChannel("BUZZGAIN", ch))
    Else
        BzGainRanged(ch, v)

Def BzGainRanged(ch As Number, v As Number) As RckWork
    If v < 0 Or v > 1 Then
        RckWorkBad("BUZZGAIN: LOUDNESS RUNS FROM 0 TO 1")
    Else
        BzGained(ch, v)

Def BzGained(ch As Number, v As Number) As RckWork
    SoundGain(ch, v)
    RckVals({ })

Rem The waveform is named rather than numbered, because "0" is not a
Rem thing anybody can read back off a stack — the numbers are
Rem buzzer.shoddy's own WaveSquare and friends, so they cannot drift.
Def BzWave(vs As List Of Cell) As RckWork
    Select Case Pair(RckWholeArg("BUZZWAVE", Nth(vs, 1)), RckTextArg("BUZZWAVE", Nth(vs, 2)))
        Case Pair(Ok(ch), Ok(name))
            BzWaveAt(ch, Lower(name))
        Case Else
            RckWorkBad("BUZZWAVE needs a channel and a waveform name")

Def BzWaveAt(ch As Number, name As String) As RckWork
    If BzWhyChannel("BUZZWAVE", ch) <> "" Then
        RckWorkBad(BzWhyChannel("BUZZWAVE", ch))
    Else
        BzWaveNamed(ch, name, BzWaveOf(name))

Def BzWaveOf(name As String) As Number
    If name = "square" Then
        WaveSquare()
    Else
        If name = "triangle" Then
            WaveTriangle()
        Else
            If name = "sine" Then
                WaveSine()
            Else
                0 - 1

Def BzWaveNamed(ch As Number, name As String, k As Number) As RckWork
    If k < 0 Then
        RckWorkBad("BUZZWAVE: \"" & name & "\" IS NOT A WAVEFORM — THEY ARE \"square\", \"triangle\" AND \"sine\"")
    Else
        BzWaved(ch, k)

Def BzWaved(ch As Number, k As Number) As RckWork
    SoundWave(ch, k)
    RckVals({ })

Rem ---- the seed ------------------------------------------------------------

Def RckSeedBuzzer(st As RckState) As RckState
    BzSeedPlay(RckSeeding(st, "seed-buzzer"))
